# Items 10 and 11 (timed input) are left out. The acceptance runner has
# no clock: a timed read runs its interrupt routine once and then takes
# the script's key, and the stream front end does not advertise timed
# input. TerpEtude therefore reports the interrupt call as WRONG, which
# describes the replay convention, not the interpreter. Timed input is
# checked at the terminal instead.

